{"name":"Pink Lemonade","hex":"#ffeaeb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink lemonade","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Lemonade coloured with the juice of red fruits such as raspberries or cherries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink_lemonade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemonade","blocks":[{"text":"Lemonade is a sweetened lemon-flavored drink that may be carbonated or un-carbonated; when carbonated, it is sometimes called a lemon soda. There are many varieties of lemonade found throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg/330px-Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemonade","wikidata":"Q893"},{"title":"List of The Pink Panther cartoons","blocks":[{"text":"This is a list of the original 124 Pink Panther animated shorts produced between December 18, 1964, and February 1, 1980, by DePatie–Freleng Enterprises for release by United Artists. The initial 92 shorts were primarily released theatrically. These entries subsequently appeared on Saturday mornings via The Pink Panther Show under the same umbrella title starting in 1969 on NBC. All 32 made-for-television entries were distributed to theaters after initially airing on The Pink Panther Show under the title The All New Pink Panther Show in 1978 on ABC, three of which were reissues of former shorts with new music cues. Every short in the series has the word pink in the title."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_The_Pink_Panther_cartoons","wikidata":"Q1613559"},{"title":"Pink Lemonade (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pink Lemonade\" is a song recorded by English singer-songwriter James Bay, from his second studio album, Electric Light (2018). The song was released by Republic Records on 7 March 2018 as the second single off the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5d/Pink_Lemonade_by_James_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Lemonade_(song)","wikidata":"Q55517027"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG/500px-R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG/1280px-R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG/500px-R_Whites_lemonade_%282%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AR_Whites_lemonade_(2).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Children_selling_lemonade_to_an_adult_in_La_Canada%2C_California%2C_1960.jpg/500px-Children_selling_lemonade_to_an_adult_in_La_Canada%2C_California%2C_1960.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Children_selling_lemonade_to_an_adult_in_La_Canada%2C_California%2C_1960.jpg/500px-Children_selling_lemonade_to_an_adult_in_La_Canada%2C_California%2C_1960.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&